{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/44381-wolf-and-spider","id":44381,"title":"Wolf and Spider","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-07T13:08:05-08:00","id":44381,"title":"Wolf and Spider","content":"&quot;Stupid little wolf.&quot; The bear-sized spider crawled down the web, its footfalls barely plucking a silken strand. &quot;Stupid little wolf,&quot; it hissed again. Its chelicerae clacked together as it eyed the green-eyed wolf bound in its web, draped like a veil over the old sawmill entrance. &quot;Howl. They can't hear you. They can't free you.&quot; At her command, thousands of spiders, many of them young Azlu, crawled over the webs in a tide of scurrying legs.<br /> <br /> No-Moon's-Song looked up at the hulking monstrosity, its once-human features melting away into hairy pedipalps, dripping fangs, half a dozen glittering eyes. At least ten shriveled forms bound in silver dotted the web. Spirits, captured and drained of Essence by an arachnid abomination. &quot;Why here?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Azarath's voiced seethed with disgust. &quot;Here, men transformed nature. Life into cold tools. Spirits come to fight. Nature and <i>un</i>nature. Men leave. My webs catch many.&quot; Its dripping mouth parts rubbed together and Song had the distinct feeling it was smiling. &quot;Catch you.&quot;<br /> <br /> No-Moon's-Song struggled uselessly against the webs. Held fast, she growled up at the approaching monster. &quot;You should have left yourself somewhere to escape,&quot; she said.<br /> <br /> A whistling shriek escaped the Azarath's chelicerae. &quot;Escape? This is <i>my </i>domain. You are <i>my </i>prey.&quot;<br /> <br /> The smell of smoke drifted to Song's sensitive nose. Her upper lip curled back in a lupine smile of her own. &quot;You are certainly strong, Broodmother. But you've grown fat in your rule.&quot;<br /> <br /> Greasy hairs rippled along the great spider's legs. It uttered a screeching wail.<br /> <br /> <i>Guess she smells it now, too.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;My pack is already burning this place down. You won't be able to escape in time. All your webs outside are already down. Only way out is through us.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Azarath surged forth, its whole body quivering with cold fury. &quot;You <i>stupid </i>little wolf! <i>You </i>won't escape either!&quot; It charged, trying to seize the werewolf in its terrible claws.<br /> <br /> As she willed the moon-magic into her body, No-Moon's-Song melted through the webbing, falling easily to the floor below. Even as she landed on four feet she stood up on two, muscles growing, claws extending to knife-length, Rage pulsing out to shake the webs. She let out a shuddering howl. &quot;I never planned to!&quot;<br /> <br /> Fire licked at the walls outside the sawmill. Monsters clashed within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 04-02-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:39:31-08:00","id":44445,"title":"","content":"Another nice piece!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:00:18-08:00","id":44498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cCurious are you? Delightful.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> <br /> Water, what can you do with it? Takes no shape, moves constantly, even changes form. Only when you put it in glass can you use it. It's chaos. That's what came before: Chaos. No shapes, no names, not even desire. Everything that could ever be, was, all at once, and changing constantly, flowing here and there. I do not mean all things, like this glass, like those creatures. I mean all things, smashed into parts and stirred together; an absolute mess. You can't work with that. You can't get anything useful, anything </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">meaningful</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> from that. And so it was sifted, by the Spinner. Little by little, she made sense of Life. She wove the Walls that sorted this from that, potential from piecemeal, blood from hunger, form from will. As she wove, two worlds began to form from the separated parts of life: one of flesh and form and sensation, one of spirit and purpose and desire. And they both grew, no longer confused with the intermingling of Everything. Form can now behave with rules, can reconstitute into something meaningful and elegant and useful. Purpose, likewise, can be shaped, refined, accumulated until ideals take shape. She wove Order into the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Her work is not complete. The Wolf murdered her. It is a slow process, creating order from chaos; until it is complete, things will continue to become confused. The Wolf was confused with rage. Unfocused, uncontrolled, unaware; a madness, like chaos, which tore things apart. She was sifting that, trying to separate out the pieces that made that chaos and place them where they could grow, and, being a powerful monster, he bit the hand of reason and tore her to pieces. She shattered, like fracturing glass, and the pieces scattered over creation. Not all is lost, for in each one of us is such a shard. Her work might not be complete, but it yet can be. Order, at last, can be made of this world. It starts by putting the pieces back together. Let me show you...\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:09:57-08:00","id":44510,"title":"","content":"Ooh, hey, I really like this and the Beshilu one. They provide an interesting perspective on why the <i>shartha </i>were wronged, and how the Wolf is unreasonable. Which is cool. Clashing myths, clashing fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}